ult_digest": "9a9b9f9ea3e85a90", "result_summary": "{\"connected\": true, \"n_events_u_to_v\": 0, \"n_events_v_to_u\": 1, \"u\": 1673, \"v\": 511, \"window\": [14821, 53221]}", "latency_ms": 0, "tokens_before": 45267, "tokens_after": 45267, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_fd7e502f", "decision": "absent", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [318, 480], "window": [14821, 53221], "confidence": 0.91, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "No time-respecting route carries influence from 318 to 480 in [14821,53221]. Under the 600-unit relay constraint, 318's temporal horizon covers only 21 nodes and yields zero paths to 480. This is not a threshold effect: at max_wait=3000 the horizon grows to 104 nodes, and with no wait limit at all it reaches 816 nodes, yet 480 remains unreachable in every case, so the ordering of timestamps \u2014 not the waiting tolerance \u2014 is what blocks the cascade. Data sparsity is ruled out, since the window holds 8,136 events over 7,980 distinct edges and both endpoints are steadily active (318: 23 events, 480: 20) across all eight time bins. The tempting positive signal is purely static: the two 2-hop neighbourhoods overlap via high-degree hubs, and a short undirected chain 318-1673-511-734-480 exists, but 1673's link to 511 actually runs 511->1673 (wrong direction) and no ascending timestamp sequence traverses it. Hub popularity and time-ignoring adjacency thus manufacture a connection that vanishes under temporal ordering. The reverse query 480->318 also fails, excluding a swapped source/target. Conclusion: connected in aggregate, but no genuine cascade."}, "raw_final_response": "**Conclusion: no time-respecting cascade exists from 318 to 480.**\n\nKey findings:\n- **Constrained reachability fails** (step_01): with max_wait \u2264 600, 318 reaches only 21 nodes; 480 is not among them. No paths enumerated at all (step_10).\n- **Not a threshold artifact**: relaxing to max_wait = 3000 expands the reachable set to 104 nodes, still excluding 480 (step_11); removing the wait constraint entirely reaches 816 nodes and *still* fails (step_04). The failure is structural in time-order, not a tuning artifact.\n- **Not a sparsity/inactivity artifact** (confounder control): the window is dense (8,136 events, 7,980 distinct edges, step_02), and both endpoints are genuinely active \u2014 318 has 23 events/23 partners, 480 has 20/20 (step_03), spread across all eight time bins (step_08).\n- **Static connectivity is the confounder** (confounder control): ignoring time, the 2-hop neighborhoods overlap through hubs (steps 05, 09), and a short static chain exists \u2014 318\u21921673 (step_13), 1673\u2194511 (step_14), with 511 and 734 being high-degree hubs (511: 144 events/123 partners; 734: 63/59, step_12) adjacent to 480 (step_06). But the 1673\u2192511 edge runs 511\u21921673, the wrong direction, and the timestamps do not ascend along any such chain. Hub popularity and undirected adjacency create the illusion of a path that time-ordering dissolves.\n- **Reverse direction also fails** (step_07), ruling out a mis-specified source/target.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_fd7e502f\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [318, 480],\n  \"window\": [14821, 53221],\n  \"confidence\": 0.91,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"No time-respecting route carries influence from 318 to 480 in [14821,53221]. Under the 600-unit relay constraint, 318's temporal horizon covers only 21 nodes and yields zero paths to 480. This is not a threshold effect: at max_wait=3000 the horizon grows to 104 nodes, and with no wait limit at all it reaches 816 nodes, yet 480 remains unreachable in every case, so the ordering of timestamps \u2014 not the waiting tolerance \u2014 is what blocks the cascade. Data sparsity is ruled out, since the window holds 8,136 events over 7,980 distinct edges and both endpoints are steadily active (318: 23 events, 480: 20) across all eight time bins. The tempting positive signal is purely static: the two 2-hop neighbourhoods overlap via high-degree hubs, and a short undirected chain 318-1673-511-734-480 exists, but 1673's link to 511 actually runs 511->1673 (wrong direction) and no ascending timestamp sequence traverses it. Hub popularity and time-ignoring adjacency thus manufacture a connection that vanishes under temporal ordering. The reverse query 480->318 also fails, excluding a swapped source/target. Conclusion: connected in aggregate, but no genuine cascade.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 56632, "total_output_tokens": 4344, "total_tokens": 60976, "total_latency_ms": 59678, "llm_calls": 7, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}